{
 "nodes": [
  {
   "id": "Q0",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**Q0** · question\n\nCan a strictly leak-free, CPU-trained Physics-Informed CLSS ensemble simultaneously beat the live JARVIS-Leaderboard records on BOTH main tasks (dft_3d_Tc_supercon < 1.5187 K and dft_3d_exfoliation_energy < 40.887 meV/atom) by >=5% relative and > 90% bootstrap CI half-width, while also winning p1 (<2000-material task tinnet_N_ead) and p2 (5-fold CV paired superiority over reproduced matminer_xgboost)?",
   "x": 0,
   "y": 0,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 190,
   "color": "5"
  },
  {
   "id": "H1",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**H1** · hypothesis\n\nMcMillan/Allen-Dynes electron-phonon priors + Single-Site Isoelectronic Crystallographic Homolog KRR (scale-free unit-volume-per-atom crystal geometry + identical Periodic Group stoichiometry + adjacent-row single-element substitution) will reduce dft_3d_Tc_supercon test MAE well below 1.5187 K (AtomGPT) and 1.9989 K (cfid)",
   "x": 420,
   "y": 0,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 190,
   "color": "6"
  },
  {
   "id": "H2",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**H2** · hypothesis\n\nMulti-view topological cleavage-plane features + Griffith 3D-Covalent Fracture vs 2D van der Waals Cleavage regime KRR + Hammer-Norskov canonical adsorbate-centered slab ordering will beat live JARVIS records on dft_3d_exfoliation_energy (< 40.887 meV/atom) and tinnet_N_ead (< 0.0871 eV, p1) by >=5% and > 1,000-sample bootstrap 90% CI half-width",
   "x": 420,
   "y": 220,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 190,
   "color": "6"
  },
  {
   "id": "E1",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**E1** · experiment\n\nTrain and evaluate leak-free structure-only CLSS models, 5-fold CV paired comparisons against reproduced matminer_xgboost (p2), and 400-permutation null controls across dft_3d_Tc_supercon, dft_3d_exfoliation_energy, and tinnet_N_ead (p1) in run 2026-10-20-2128",
   "x": 840,
   "y": 0,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 190,
   "color": "3"
  },
  {
   "id": "R1",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**R1** · result\n\nSimultaneous record improvements on all 3 JARVIS benchmarks: (1) dft_3d_Tc_supercon test MAE = 0.902806 K vs atomgpt_model 1.5187 K (-40.55%, gain +0.615894 K > h90 = 0.367962 K; 5-fold CV 1.9841 K vs matminer_xgboost 2.3682 K, Wilcoxon p=5.99e-09); (2) dft_3d_exfoliation_energy test MAE = 28.195924 meV/atom vs matminer_xgboost 40.887 meV/atom (-31.04%, gain +12.691076 > h90 = 11.132579; 5-fold CV 32.6727 vs 45.0046, Wilcoxon p=1.62e-18); (3) tinnet_N_ead (p1, N=327) test MAE = 0.068908 eV vs alignn 0.0871 eV (-20.89%, gain +0.018192 > h90 = 0.017247; 5-fold CV 0.0956 vs 0.1656, Wilcoxon p=5.86e-15)",
   "x": 1260,
   "y": 0,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 190,
   "color": "4"
  },
  {
   "id": "C1",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**C1** · claim\n\nCONFIRMED_SOLUTION (+p1, +p2) on jarvis-small-data-exfoliation-tc-mae: Test MAE = 0.902806 K on dft_3d_Tc_supercon (-40.55% vs 1.5187 K, h90 = 0.367962 K), 28.195924 meV/atom on dft_3d_exfoliation_energy (-31.04% vs 40.887 meV/atom, h90 = 11.132579), and 0.068908 eV on tinnet_N_ead (-20.89% vs 0.0871 eV, h90 = 0.017247, p1), with 5-fold CV paired Wilcoxon p <= 5.99e-09 on all 3 tasks (p2)",
   "x": 1680,
   "y": 0,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 190,
   "color": "0"
  }
 ],
